{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/986808-example-of-a-materialized-spirit","id":986808,"title":"Example of a Materialized Spirit?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-13T09:37:11-07:00","id":986808,"title":"Example of a Materialized Spirit?","content":"I'm trying to understand how to create a spirit that has materialized using the rules in M20 on p493:<br /> <br /> Materialize: This Charm allows a spirit to assume physical shape in the material world\u2026 a dangerous thing, especially in the age of machine-gun fire. To do so, the spirit\u2019s Gnosis must be higher than the local Gauntlet rating. Once materialized, the spirit can go wherever it wants to go, provided that the local Gauntlet rating is no higher than the spirit\u2019s Gnosis -2, and assuming<br /> that no one has bound that spirit in a mystic pentacle or hypertech spirit cage (in game terms, a Spirit 4 Effect; see the Spirit Sphere entry in Chapter Ten.) If the entity gets killed in the material realm, its form is dispersed and the spirit winds up banished to the Umbra in Slumber, as if its Essence had been dispersed in the spirit realm.<br /> <br /> Under the old World of Darkness rules, a materialized spirit had to buy its Physical Attributes, health levels, and Abilities per the chart below. (A materialized spirit still uses its Gnosis for Social and Mental Attributes.) This approach allows a spirit to expand its capabilities, so long as it has enough Essence to do so. Alternately, the spirit can simply manifest and use its Willpower, Rage, Gnosis, and Essence as usual, without bothering to generate Attributes and Abilities, as per Werewolf: The Apocalypse 20 th Anniversary Edition. In that case, however, the spirit remains bound to a single form in the Earthly realm and cannot adjust its size or capabilities. The spirits in Appendix I have been built using the physical forms suggested by the older rules.<br /> <br /> Typically, a spirit soaks damage with its Willpower Trait, plus the Armor Charm if it has that power. When a materialized spirit gets hit, however, the Stamina Trait (plus armor) soaks damage if that Trait is higher than Willpower. To a materialized spirit entity, bashing, lethal, and aggravated damage are essentially the same \u2013 all three drain Essence points if they manage to inflict damage against the spirit\u2019s body. If that spirit takes damage, its materialized health levels absorb the damage first; once those health levels are gone, the spirit can take up to five more health levels in damage before its Essence dissipates back into the Umbra. Whether or not the dead materialized husk remains behind after the spirit\u2019s Essence has departed is a Storyteller call. Given the long histories of \u201cdemon\u2019s blood,\u201d \u201cangel feathers,\u201d and \u201cdead alien bodies,\u201d however, tradition suggests that a corpse should remain behind.<br /> <br /> Essence Cost Trait<br /> 5 Initial manifestation (Paradox spirits do not pay this cost).<br /> 1 Per one Physical Attribute level.<br /> 1 Per two Ability levels.<br /> 1 Seven initial health levels.<br /> 1 Per additional health levels (each extra health level also increases size).<br /> 1 Weaponry; per die of aggravated damage above Strength damage.<br /> 1 Per physical health level healed.<br /> <br /> Do the rules above mean that a spirit pays 1 essence for each dot in it's physical attributes and 1 essence for each 2 dots in abilities? The use of the word 'level' seems ambiguous here.<br /> e.g. A materialized spirit with Strength 3, Dexterity 3, Stamina 3 and Brawl 2 would cost 10 essence?<br /> <br /> Regarding taking damage it seems that a materialized spirit will soak damage as above taking damage against it's seven (or more) health levels (I assume it also takes the penalties for damage?) Once it has taken seven levels does it then discorporate becoming immaterial and able to take another five levels or does it just lie there incapacitated until it takes five more damage and then dissipates?<br /> <br /> Are there any examples of this as to how it plays out? I'm having trouble going from rules in the book to how it would work in a game session.<br /> <br /> Or is it meant to be vague so that you can just wing it as a GM?<br /> <br /> p.s. How would you record all this in a stat block? e.g.<br /> <br /> <b>Materialized Example Spirit (5 essence)</b> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Attributes:</b> Strength 3, Dexterity 3, Stamina 3 (9 essence)</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Abilities:</b> Brawl 2 (1 essence)</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Willpower:</b> 6</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Rage</b>: 7</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Gnosis</b>: 5</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Essence</b>: (40 - 17) 23</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Health Levels:</b> OK, -1, -1, -2, -2, -5, Incapacitated (1 essence)</span><br /> <b>Attacks</b>: Claws 4 aggravated (1 essence)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T18:03:34-07:00","id":987018,"title":"","content":"Your understanding seems pretty good actually. The Essence cost is pretty much as you stated. When it comes to manifested health levels, they are basically like any other character. If you have damage up to incapacitated, then you're incapacitated. If you get lethal damage up to and over, then that's the end of your body. For a spirit this means their manifestation ends and they fall into slumber. A spirit can heal it's health levels with further essence points pretty much whenever it wants. Also, if they give themselves physical attributes, they replace the use of Willpower and Rage for fighting and damage, thought Willpower will still be used for certain things (as normal willpower might be used).<br /> <br /> I'm not sure is spirits have penalties for low health levels. They aren't really getting hurt so much as losing connection to their manifested forms. But it's your call if you'd rather they have health levels.<br /> <br /> The quick and dirty way is to just have their Willpower and Rage be their primary stats along with Gnosis, and then make Essence their health levels. I prefer this way because it's just a lot fewer stats to keep track of.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T19:33:48-07:00","id":987063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/986808-example-of-a-materialized-spirit?p=987018#post987018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">..The quick and dirty way is to just have their Willpower and Rage be their primary stats along with Gnosis, and then make Essence their health levels. I prefer this way because it's just a lot fewer stats to keep track of.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why not use both?<br /> <br /> The quick and dirty &quot;spirits have 3 stats&quot; way for when a spirit wants to use its full power(after all, with only 3 stats spirits can become very powerful if you allow NPCs to gain experience in chronicles). The spirit can then have beyond 5 level stats very easily, more health levels than a normal creature can usually store, and full access to all its charms. On the other hand the spirits also draws from its own health whenever it uses its powers and getting into a rough fight will weaken the spirit for a long time afterwards even if it wins.<br /> <br /> The spirit also then has the option to create a material body. Doing so allows the spirit free access to its essence without killing or discorporating itself(after all its health is now a separate stat), access to abilities and weapons that don't use up its essence, and a way to hide among to populace(after all, no one's going to look twice at a random cat or stranger on the street. the angelic manifestation of healing on the other hand...). The downside is that making a body is expensive on essence, your stats and abilities are limited(likely less then 5 do to cost), you probably have restrictions on some of your charms(like how wraiths can't manifest some powers as risen), and you are a lot squishier health-wise if you don't burn the essence to heal in combat.<br /> <br /> In a way it could be a lot like DTF. with some spirits manifested in material forms to blend in, until sufficiently threatened, in which case they shift into their true form and start breaking things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T10:47:57-07:00","id":987331,"title":"","content":"Thanks guys that's helped a lot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}